WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.280
A little later in the course, we are going&nbsp;
to be covering SQL keywords. Before we do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.480
though, you can get a decent SQL reference on a&nbsp;
table by generating the statement necessary to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.160
create the table. I will select and hold (or&nbsp;
right-click) this Person.EmailAddress table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:27.760
then select Script Table as, CREATE to, and&nbsp;
New Query Editor Window. Once this is done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:36.720
we see the syntax for the columns added to the&nbsp;
table and the primary key, which, as we see here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:43.840
is a constraint with the two fields we saw&nbsp;
earlier, BusinessEntityID and EmailAddressID.

